etimes these  decisions need to be taken quickly  well we understand why decisions have to  be taken quickly you have to act with  speed when responding to a pandemic and  one of the  one of the big criticisms of the  government which  is broadly accepted now across the board  isn't it that the government were too  slow in their response to the pandemic  even though  the pandemic was the number one issue on  our risk register  we know they were too slow to put in the  supports and protections for care homes  even though many people were warning  that social care we're talking now  i know we're talking about um spain but  i mean the point is  generally throughout the crisis the  government's response has been  slow and we've always urged them to act  quickly so look i don't  i understand why they've made this  decision about spain  in the last 24 hours this virus is on  the increase in countries across the  world we've got some countries  uh even talking about going back into  national lockdowns  for example so it's a reminder that we  cannot be complacent about this virus  but the way in which this was  communicated i mean it broke on twitter  because a a sunday journalist a very  good sunday journalist got hold of the  story  and then the government had to scramble  to confirm it that is no way to treat  people  who are currently on holiday in spain  are about to go on holiday with their  families to spain is it  as you say um i think a lot of people  will be thinking twice about any foreign  summer holiday  they've got butch even grant chaps the  transport secretary caught in his own  lockdown  have you got a foreign holiday booked  you planning a staycation or do you feel  a bit sorry for mr shafts  well i mean you couldn't make it up that  grand chaps is over there  on holiday in spain when he's the  transport secretary i think that tells  you everything about  uh the sort of the governments approach  this but personally  i mean we're here in lockdown here in  l