ting advice and  encouraging people to take up cycling  and even prescribing cycling  uh on the nhs so it's not clear how much  money they're putting into that that  project  dieting advice and encouraging people  with exercise is obviously a good thing  and  actually labour's manifesto last year  talks about encouraging people to take  up cycling and giving people support to  take up cycling  but tackling obesity is it has to be a  much  wider approach you've got to tackle the  circumstances in which people live the  environment  in which people live i mean there is a  correlation between poverty and  inequality  and obesity the poorest spend a greater  proportion of their income  on food but it's often low nutritional  food because that's  cheaper so we need to give people  support to buy healthier healthier food  but the government have cut the health  the healthy start food vouchers  and to be frank it shouldn't take a man  united footballer and labour and  peace to bring the government kicking  and screaming  to give families food vouchers  throughout the summer  but we're also going to take on what i  call the commercial determinants of ill  health  i mean why are we allowing junk food to  be advertised  on pre-watershed tv two years ago  torrey ministers came to the house of  commons when jeremy hunt was the health  secretary at the time they came to the  house of commons and said they were  going to stop this  and then they just kicked it into the  long grass with consultation after  consultation  we need decisive action so look dieting  advice is great  ex more exercise more more cycling yeah  that's a good thing  but we need action around uh accessing  nutritional food we need to ban junk  food advertising  we need to give families support we need  to give people health  healthy start vouchers not cut them and  also these high energy drinks that kids  can buy in shops  i mean why aren't we banning that kids  shouldn't be buying high energy drinks  in shops