ample and fighting to improve our  economy so it's a fairer economy  and people can get a decent wage packet  at the end of the month and we invest in  people by giving them skills  for the future i think that was the  right thing to do and i think you'll  find there were  many occasions when i kept came on your  program or another on other  uh programs and i spoke out against  anti-semitism i said we need to go  further and faster  in the labour party and kierstama is  absolutely right  to be saying that anti-semitism has no  place  in the labour party it is a poison and  we'll do  absolutely everything to move this to  shift this to push this out  of the labour party and challenge  anti-semitism not just in the labour  party but whenever we come across it  in society which is why for example i  was very pleased that our shadow culture  secretary yesterday  was very forthright on calling out  twitter because twitter has been  absolutely appalling in the last 24  hours  in refusing to take on the anti-semitic  vile poison that we've seen coming out  of that particular  grime artist i mean this is what we mean  when we say we take on anti-semitism we  stand against anti-semitism  in every circumstance whenever we come  across it and in every circumstance

